  ('taming-the-paperwork-pile', 8, 'Pick one letter from today''s mail that takes less than two minutes, and deal with it before you sit down.'),
  ('taming-the-paperwork-pile', 9, 'Choose one sturdy folder or envelope to become the home for your most important papers.'),
  ('taming-the-paperwork-pile', 10, 'Plan your next paper session around something you look forward to, like a call with a friend afterward.'),
  ('taming-the-paperwork-pile', 11, 'Walk through your home with a tote bag and drop in every stray envelope you spot on counters and tables.'),
  ('taming-the-paperwork-pile', 12, 'Set the tray on a table or shelf you pass every evening, so dropping papers there feels natural.'),
  ('taming-the-paperwork-pile', 13, 'Set aside a few minutes after the mail comes to look at each envelope''s sender before you decide what to do.'),
